A building plan gives a rectangular roof as $9600$ mm by $7500$ mm. During a storm, $15$ mm of rain falls on it. Find the volume of rainfall on the roof in litres.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (9.6,7.5);
\path (4.8,0) node[below] {$9600\text{ mm}$};
\path (9.6,3.75) node[right] {$7500\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular roof measures $3.5$ cm by $2$ cm on a plan drawn to a scale of $1:600$. If $25$ mm of rain falls, find the volume collected in litres. Assume all rainfall on the roof is collected.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=15mm,y=15mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (3.5,2);
\path (1.75,0) node[below] {$3.5\text{ cm}$};
\path (3.5,1) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The L-shaped roof plan has scale $1:300$. A storm drops $18$ mm of rain. Find the volume of water collected in kilolitres, assuming all rainfall on the roof is collected.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,2)--(3,2)--(3,4)--(0,4)--cycle;
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (5,1) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (4,2) node[above] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (3,3) node[right] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.5,4) node[above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,2) node[left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
